      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey im working in a jupyter notebook and im getting this annoying SettingWithCopyWarning when i try to add a new column to a dataframe that i sliced from a bigger one. can u tell me why this happens and how i can fix it properly?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The `SettingWithCopyWarning` warning occurs when you try to modify a slice of a DataFrame (i.e., assign to the result of `df.loc[]` or `df.iloc[]`). This is because the slice creates a new DataFrame, and you're trying to modify the original DataFrame from the slice, not the original DataFrame. \n\nTo avoid this warning, you can call the operations on the original DataFrame's copy, which you can create by prefixing it with a `.copy()` attribute, like so: `df.loc[:, 'new_column'] = df.loc[:, 'old_column'].copy()`. Alternatively, you can also reassign the result back to the original DataFrame: `df = df.loc[:, 'new_column'] = ...`.",
      "source": "target",
